
System & Console Commands
console.log(message); Prints a message or interpolated string to the output console window.

Example: console.log("System Ready!");

Interpolation: console.log($"Player Name: {this.Name}");

Task.sleep(milliseconds); Pauses non-blocking execution asynchronously for a specified duration.

Example: await Task.sleep(500);


2D Engine Rendering Commands
Use these commands to render graphics directly onto the 2D Game Display:

Canvas.drawRect(x, y, width, height); Renders a rectangle on the 2D viewport at (x, y).

Example: Canvas.drawRect(this.X, this.Y, 30, 30);

Canvas.drawCircle(x, y, radius); Renders a circle at the specified coordinates.

Example: Canvas.drawCircle(100, 150, 20);

Canvas.clear(); Clears all active shapes on the 2D canvas.



Interactive Input Bindings
When running a 2D application in J# Studio, the viewport captures key presses automatically:

Movement Commands: W, A, S, D or Up, Down, Left, Right Arrow keys update the active canvas frame.

Auto-Complete Command: Press Tab or Enter inside the code editor to auto-complete keywords and commands.

